### Summary

When a chat agent sends a message mid-work and then keeps working, that message gets hidden inside the collapsed "Completed N steps" section after the response finishes. It shows again only if you click to expand that section.

Expected: the message stays visible; only the work steps (thinking, tool calls) should be collapsed.

### Repro

A chat participant emitting parts in this order: thinking → tool → markdown reply → tool → final markdown answer.

```ts
import * as vscode from 'vscode';

export function activate(context: vscode.ExtensionContext): void {
	context.subscriptions.push(vscode.chat.createChatParticipant('repro.collapse', async (_request, stream) => {
		// Work step 1: thinking
		stream.thinkingProgress({ text: 'Analyzing the issue...', id: 'thinking-1' });

		// Work step 2: tool
		const tool1 = new vscode.ChatToolInvocationPart('my_tool', 'tool-1');
		tool1.isComplete = true;
		tool1.isConfirmed = true;
		stream.push(tool1);

		// Intermediate reply - gets collapsed and hidden
		stream.markdown('I will check the error handling approach.');

		// Work step 3: tool
		const tool2 = new vscode.ChatToolInvocationPart('my_tool', 'tool-2');
		tool2.isComplete = true;
		tool2.isConfirmed = true;
		stream.push(tool2);

		// Final answer
		stream.markdown('Here is the final answer.');

		return { metadata: {} };
	}));
}
```
The setting `chat.collapseCompletedResponses` should be enabled (default on in Insiders), and `enabledApiProposals: ["chatParticipantAdditions"]` in the extension's `package.json`.

<img width="383" height="269" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb692593-70f3-448d-8994-35fc2cb06ac7" />

### Root cause

`shouldCollapseCompletedResponsePart` in `src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts` treated every part except MCP-app tool invocations as collapsible, including `markdownContent`, so `getCompletedResponseCollapseEndIndex` walked past intermediate markdown replies and folded them into the disclosure.

### Fix

Exclude `markdownContent` from the collapsible set:

```diff
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts
@@ -376,6 +376,13 @@ export function formatResponseTokenStats(modelTotals: readonly IChatUsageModelTo
 }

 export function shouldCollapseCompletedResponsePart(part: IChatRendererContent): boolean {
+       // Intermediate replies are user-visible content, not work steps: never fold
+       // markdown into the completed-response disclosure. Otherwise an agent that
+       // replies mid-flight (e.g. "I'll check the error handling...") would have
+       // that reply hidden alongside thinking parts when the response completes.
+       if (part.kind === 'markdownContent') {
+               return false;
+       }
        return (part.kind !== 'toolInvocation' && part.kind !== 'toolInvocationSerialized') || !toolInvocationHasMcpAppData(part)
;
 }
```

